    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Alice measures her half of an entangled pair, and Bob's conditional state can be updated instantly. But Bob sees no controllable change. Entanglement alone cannot carry a message.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Show why entanglement correlations cannot transmit a message.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — NO SIGNALING",
            "segment": "Bob's Local Statistics",
            "greeting": "Olá, Liam",
            "runningText": "separating conditional states from local data…",
            "output": [
              "Alice changes correlations and conditional ensembles.",
              "Bob's unconditioned local distribution stays fixed."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Let Alice and Bob share a Bell pair. If both measure the same basis, their outcomes show a perfect pattern when the records are compared.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "split"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Before comparison, Bob's own results are random: zero half the time and one half the time. A random string carries no chosen bit from Alice.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Suppose Alice measures Z. If she gets zero, Bob's conditional Z state is zero; if she gets one, his conditional state is one. Alice cannot choose which outcome occurs.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Average over Alice's unknown outcome and Bob still sees fifty-fifty. His local Bloch vector remains at the center.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "If Alice instead measures X, Bob's conditional states are plus or minus. But Bob measuring locally, without Alice's result, still receives the same maximally mixed statistics.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Alice may also apply a local unitary or do nothing. Any local trace-preserving operation, with outcomes ignored, leaves Bob's reduced state unchanged.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Postselecting one of Alice's outcomes can define a different conditional ensemble for Bob. But Bob cannot know which runs belong to it until Alice sends the outcome through an ordinary classical channel.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "That classical comparison reveals the nonclassical joint pattern and can violate a Bell inequality. It arrives no faster than the communication channel carrying the records.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "The instant update is therefore an update to a conditional description, not a usable local signal appearing in Bob's detector counts.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Alice switches between Z and X measurements. Can Bob infer her choice from his local outcomes alone? Pause before the answer: no. Both choices leave his unconditioned local state maximally mixed.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: can Bob identify Alice's basis locally?",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Marginal Versus Correlation",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the local-statistics test…",
            "output": [
              "Bob alone: identical 50/50 statistics.",
              "After classical comparison: basis-dependent correlations."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Entanglement cannot send a message: the surprise lives in the comparison, not in either local data stream alone.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "fade"
